        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Make the incline the variable, and slow down when you raise
            it.</strong> Hill repeats once a week, rolling hills for variety, a progressive climb
            for pacing and long incline walks as the easy base cover almost everything a home
            runner or walker needs.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Judge effort by breathing rather than pace, build one variable at a time to protect your
            calves and Achilles, and keep off the rails. For the steady fixed version, see the
            <a href="/12-3-30-treadmill-workout/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">12-3-30 workout</a>
            — and remember the descents still have to be practised outdoors.
          </p>
